course: dictionary
lesson: 11648
title: The word articulate
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Articulate has more than one meaning, so the words around it show you which one to use. «Mia is an articulate speaker. She explains her ideas clearly and well.» Here articulate is an adjective. It describes someone who can say what they think in clear words.
explain: Articulate can also be a verb, a doing word. «Mia articulated her idea so clearly that everyone understood.» To articulate an idea is to express it clearly in words. «Say each sound clearly» uses the same idea for sounds: to articulate a sound is to say it clearly.
explain: Some meanings have nothing to do with speaking. «The skeleton's arms are articulated, so the bones can bend at the joints.» Here articulated means joined so the parts can move. «The articulated lorry turned the corner.» An articulated lorry is a long lorry that bends in the middle. The sentence is about joints or bending, not words, so the clues tell you the meaning.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. Does «Mia is a clear speaker» still make sense? Then articulate means clear in speaking. When you are still unsure, look the word up in a dictionary.
fact: Articulate can be an adjective: an articulate person can express ideas clearly and well in words.
fact: Articulate can be a verb: to articulate ideas or feelings is to say them clearly in words.
fact: To articulate sounds is to say them clearly, so that every sound can be heard.
fact: In science, to articulate means to join parts with a joint so they can move, like bones.
fact: An «articulated lorry» is a long lorry that bends in the middle.
exercise: «Mia is very articulate when she talks about her ideas.» What does articulate mean here? | Loud and noisy | Tired after a long day | *Able to express ideas clearly in words | Shy and quiet
exercise: «The teacher asked us to articulate each word clearly.» What does articulate mean here? | Write in pencil | *Say clearly | Hide from view | Count the letters
exercise: «The skeleton's arms are articulated, so the bones can move at the joints.» What does articulated mean here? | Made of wood | Very big | *Joined so the parts can move | Painted in bright colours
test: «The articulated lorry took a sharp bend in the road.» What is an articulated lorry? | A bus for children | A boat on the river | *A long lorry that bends in the middle | A toy lorry for a shop
test: «Grandma articulated her feelings about the news in a calm, clear voice.» What does articulated mean here? | Forgot | Whispered quietly | Hid | *Expressed in clear words
exam: Which sentence uses articulate as a verb? | «He is a very articulate boy.» | «The articulated lorry was red.» | «The skeleton has articulated bones.» | *«He articulated his plan so the whole class understood.»
